INT. ROOFTOP GREENHOUSE RESTAURANT - NIGHT

A glass pavilion on top of a skyscraper. Tomato vines climb strings overhead. Candles on white tablecloths. The city glitters below like spilled sequins. Only one table is occupied.

At it sit four people.

ARCHIBALD "ARCHIE" ADEYEMI-VANCE, 60s, silver hair, bespoke suit, ring on every finger. He swirls wine and watches no one.

His daughter, ISADORA ADEYEMI-VANCE, 30s, in a red dress, sits straight, hands on the cloth. Her smile is not a smile.

Opposite her, THADDEUS "THAD" KOWALCZYK-OSEI, 40s, a lawyer, loosens his tie and sweats. His briefcase rests under his chair.

And at the head, quiet as a stone: MADAME LUCRETIA FAIRWEATHER-NNAMDI, 70s, black lace gloves, who has not spoken since the soup.

ARCHIE
The tomatoes are from the vine above us.

THAD
Impressive.

ISADORA
He says that every year.

ARCHIE
Because it's true every year.

LUCRETIA
(softly)
The knife, Archibald.

Archie glances at the steak knife by his plate. Slowly pushes it away from him.

ARCHIE
Of course.

THAD
Mr. Adeyemi-Vance, if we could return to the papers--

ISADORA
Papers.

THAD
The transfer of shares.

ARCHIE
After dessert.

ISADORA
^After dessert, Thad. Always after dessert.

Neither of them looks at the other. Lucretia lifts a finger, and the candles flicker as a gust finds the vents.

LUCRETIA
My late husband built this building. On a handshake.

THAD
So I've heard.

LUCRETIA
He would have disliked the tomatoes.

ARCHIE
Lucretia, we all have our vices.

LUCRETIA
Yours cost him forty million.

Silence. A tomato vine sways. Archie sets down his glass. Isadora folds her napkin into a neat square. Thad reaches under his chair for the briefcase.

THAD
Madame, I'm only here to--

LUCRETIA
Sit, young man.

He sits.

LUCRETIA (CONT'D)
Isadora, my dear. You may open the window.

ISADORA
Which one?

LUCRETIA
The big one.

Isadora rises. Crosses to the glass wall. Flips a latch. A section slides back and night air pours in, cold and loud with traffic far below.

ARCHIE
What are you doing?

ISADORA
Letting in a draught.

She returns to the table. Resumes her seat. Takes the steak knife from beside her father's plate and lays it across her own, perfectly aligned.

LUCRETIA
Archibald. The papers.

Archie's mouth tightens. He reaches into his jacket, draws out a folded envelope, and slides it across the cloth.
